Description: base's StackTrace uses backtrace() on Jam OS (libc has <execinfo.h>)
 base/debug/stack_trace_posix.cc takes backtrace() and backtrace_symbols()
 only where the C library is glibc (or Apple's), by __GLIBC__. Jam OS's libc
 is musl with glibc's <execinfo.h> added (user/posix/glibc/execinfo.c:
 backtrace() walks the program's own unwind tables, takes no lock and calls
 nothing, so the crash handler may call it), so the glibc path is the right
 one here: StackTrace collects frames, prints them and streams them. This
 one condition replaces Alpine's no-execinfo.patch (0001, dropped: its
 hunks only made musl's lack of <execinfo.h> compile) and our earlier 0911
 (a StackTrace::OutputToStreamWithPrefixImpl for the build without
 backtrace()). __jamos__ is defined by the Jam OS toolchain for the target
 (0901), not for the host's tools.
Forwarded: not-needed (Jam OS's: musl, static programs)
---
--- a/base/debug/stack_trace_posix.cc
+++ b/base/debug/stack_trace_posix.cc
@@ -46,8 +46,9 @@

 // Surprisingly, uClibc defines __GLIBC__ in some build configs, but
 // execinfo.h and backtrace(3) are really only present in glibc and in macOS
-// libc.
-#if BUILDFLAG(IS_APPLE) || \
+// libc. Jam OS's libc has them too (backtrace() by the program's unwind
+// tables), though it is musl and does not define __GLIBC__.
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_APPLE) || defined(__jamos__) || \
     (defined(__GLIBC__) && !defined(__UCLIBC__) && !defined(__AIX))
 #define HAVE_BACKTRACE
 #include <execinfo.h>
